  "body": "Refs #773 (item 1 of 1, 2 and 5; the other two have their own PRs)\nClaim: cloud/i773-sonnet\n\n**Problem.** Nothing checks that `tooling/fixtures/corpus.json` and the capture table of `MANIFEST.md` agree. Two re-checks (#758, #764) reported gaps by hand; both were false positives (the \"Store\" table headers, grouped rows such as `| T11, T11h |`).\n\n**Change.** `tooling/fixtures/manifest_check.py`, run in CI by the existing unit-test step of the `fixture-tooling` job (`test_committed_corpus_and_manifest_agree`). No `ci.yml` edit on purpose: `ci.yml` is in the macOS jobs' change filter, so an explicit step would start two macOS jobs on a Linux-only PR.\n- reads only the table whose header starts with `Id` (the \"Store\" tables, \"Not captured\" and the prose are ignored);\n- a grouped row names each of its ids; a row whose first cell is in parentheses (`(oracles)`, three of them today) is a pointer, not a capture;\n- fails on: a corpus id no row names, a MANIFEST id missing from the corpus, an id named twice on either side.\nIt loads the corpus through `publish.load_manifest`, so the corpus layout change of the next PR does not touch it. No change to `MANIFEST.md` or `corpus.json`: it passes on `dev-swift` today.\n\n**Tests** (`tooling/fixtures/tests/test_manifest_check.py`, written first and seen failing on the missing module): grouped rows, headers and other tables ignored, pointer rows, table end, each of the four failure kinds, CLI exit codes, and the committed files agree. A run with `T21` removed from a copy of the corpus exits 1.\n\nLinux-only (no `App/` or `Packages/` change): no macOS job.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJVVwEjUSAtcnoKNKN\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
