   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5), round 1: APPROVE** on head 44a8aa17076851c5720dcb25d7cb4d7880dfc937\n\nVerdict as returned by the reviewer, verbatim:\n\n> **Revue adversariale (Opus 5.5) : APPROUVÉ** — tête 44a8aa17076851c5720dcb25d7cb4d7880dfc937\n>\n> No Haute or Moyenne findings; the check passes on today's files (351 ids on each side), the CI step sits in `fixture-tooling` (no path filter), 3 mutations each broke 9-10 tests.\n>\n> **Constats**\n> 1. Détail — `tooling/fixtures/manifest_check.py:49,73`: a MANIFEST without an `| Id |` table ends in a Python traceback, not a `FAIL` line. Fix: catch `ValueError` in `main` and print `FAIL <message>`.\n> 2. Détail — `tests/test_manifest_check.py:125-127`: the CI step runs the same check on the real files as `test_committed_corpus_and_manifest_agree`. One redundant run, acceptable.\n> 3. Détail — `manifest_check.py:73` reads `corpus.json` directly. If item 2 of #773 splits the corpus into `corpus.d/`, this check must follow that change.\n\nHandling: 1 and 3 are fixed in one commit (the default corpus path now comes from `publish.DEFAULT_MANIFEST`, so the layout change of the corpus PR needs no edit here); 2 kept. The head changes, so a round 2 follows.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
