   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5), round 2: APPROVE** on head 77b22355eaf1f6429bd76efda3d5d01affb8f84e\n\nVerdict as returned by the reviewer, verbatim:\n\n> 1. Low — `tooling/fixtures/manifest_check.py:73-76`. `except (OSError, ValueError)` does not catch `KeyError` or `TypeError` raised by `publish.load_manifest`. Failing scenario: a corpus file `{\"x\":1}`, a missing `id`, or a `captures` that is not a list prints a `KeyError: 'captures'` traceback, not a `FAIL` line. Fix: add `KeyError, TypeError` to the except clause, plus one test.\n> 2. Detail — `manifest_check.py:4`. The usage line says `--corpus corpus.json|corpus.d`, but `corpus.d/` exists only on the open branch `chore/773-corpus-fragments`.\n>\n> Holds up: both directions checked, grouped rows count, only the `| Id |` table is read, duplicates reported on both sides, wired into `fixture-tooling` (no path filter), tests fail without the change; 354 tests OK, check rc=0 on the real files.\n\nHandling: no new commit, so the APPROVE stays on the head. Both notes disappear with #777: its `load_manifest` raises `ValueError` for a fragment without `captures`, a non-list or an entry missing a key (tested there), and it creates `corpus.d/`, which makes the usage line true.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
